// FROST FORTRESS — BLACK ICE — one song: what it plays, how it is arranged, how it sounds.
//
// FROST FORTRESS as future garage — a game alternate of frost, selectable from the dev
// menu (GAME ALTERNATES) and on the desk. Nothing replaces the live song.
// 
// Two-step at 134 with the sixteenths swung, a sub under a slow Reese, frost's own
// Polar Drift pad, a tine piano, an ice bell. The hook is RE-RHYTHMED onto a garage
// bounce — the same seven notes and arch, displaced onto the swung sixteenths — and
// sung as a vowel chop, CALL AND RESPONSE with the ice bell, which answers with the
// hook upside down. The harmony is frost's own i–IV dorian vamp, Dm9 to G9sus, with
// Bbmaj9 and Gm9 turning the phrase. In the middle the floor drops into HALF TIME:
// the original's own groove on its own kick and snare, and frost's singers
// (jmjrSmallVoice, laa) sing the hook at half speed over a D pedal. Main two moves
// D, F#, D, F# four bars at a time — the original's own form.
// 
//   1–4    intro — vowel-chop call, bell answer, pad, sub (the cabinet-screen loop)
//   5–8    groove in — the two-step and the bass arrive
//   9–24   main — call and response; the singers take a third above from bar 17
//   25–32  half time — frost's groove and kit; the hook half speed, Dm9 Gm9 Bbmaj9 Am11
//   33–48  main two — D, F#, D, F#, four bars each
//   49–52  dub — drums out, the chop and the bell into the delays
//   53–56  groove in again; the loop returns to bar 9
// 
// Cabinet sync kept: frost-3's sleigh carol takes its key from the first bass note of
// the section it lands in, so every bar pair starts on the tonic (D, or F# when
// lifted); the generator asserts it.
// 
// 56 bars at 134, swing 57, 100s. Written by
// work/local/_frost-remix-black-ice.mjs through work/local/_remix-lib.mjs;
// re-running it rewrites this file.
//
// SPOT FX — MORE (1 Oct 2026, work/local/_spot-fx-more.mjs): a delay throw on the ice bell's last answer of bar 48 (step 14), echoing into the dub.
//
// The music below is the composition. Everything under THE DESK WRITES BELOW HERE
// is written by `npm run mixer` and will be rewritten on every save — put notes
// about the song up here, where they survive.
